-- title:
--   Products of independent degree-one elements are non-zero
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $H$ a non-zero associative $k$-algebra and $H'$ an associative $k$-algebra, and let $\mathcal A : \mathbb N \to \mathrm{Submod}_k(H)$ be a family of $k$-subspaces of $H$ that is a graded monoid, i.e. $1 \in \mathcal A_0$ and $\mathcal A_a \cdot \mathcal A_b \subseteq \mathcal A_{a+b}$ for all $a,b$. Let $p_1, p_2, m : H \to H'$ be $k$-algebra homomorphisms subject to three hypotheses: (i) the $k$-linear map $\bigoplus_{(a,b) \in \mathbb N \times \mathbb N} \mathcal A_a \otimes_k \mathcal A_b \to H'$ whose $(a,b)$-component sends $u \otimes v$ to $p_1(u)\,p_2(v)$ (that is, the tensor product of the inclusions of $\mathcal A_a$ and $\mathcal A_b$ followed by $p_1 \otimes p_2$ and then multiplication in $H'$) is injective; (ii) $p_2(x)\,p_1(y) = -\,p_1(y)\,p_2(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathcal A_1$; (iii) $m(x) = p_1(x) + p_2(x)$ for all $x \in \mathcal A_1$. Then for every $n \in \mathbb N$ and every family $x : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to H$ with $x_i \in \mathcal A_1$ for all $i$ and $(x_i)_i$ linearly independent over $k$, the ordered product $x_0 x_1 \cdots x_{n-1}$ (the product of the list $\mathrm{ofFn}\,x$, equal to $1$ when $n = 0$) is non-zero in $H$.
--
--   This is the degree-one part of the Hopf–Borel structure theorem for connected graded Hopf algebras, isolated as a statement of pure algebra using only the anticommutation and primitivity relations in degree one together with injectivity of the Künneth-type multiplication map; the intended model is the coherent cohomology ring of an abelian variety, with $p_1, p_2, m$ the pull-backs along the two projections and the group law. It is the engine behind the subsequent bounds on the graded pieces, being cited in the proofs that degree-two elements vanish, that a degree-one space of dimension one forces the higher degrees to be generated by it, and in the rank bound [`SetLike.GradedMonoid.rank_le_of_eq_bot_of_kunneth_injective`](thm.html#SetLike.GradedMonoid.rank_le_of_eq_bot_of_kunneth_injective).
